Let P(x) = (1 - 3x + 3x^2)^{14} (1 + 3x - 3x^2)^{14}. Consider Q(x) to be the polynomial obtained by fully expanding P(x) and collecting like terms. What is the sum of all coefficients in Q(x)?\n\nA) 1\nB) 0\nC) 2^{14}\nD) 3^{14}

A) 1
B) 0
C) 2^{14}
D) 3^{14}

Let \( A = \begin{bmatrix} 3 & 5 \ 2 & 3 \end{bmatrix} \). Which of the following matrices, when multiplied by \( A \), will yield the identity matrix? \n\nA student computes values and arrives at possible inverses shown below. Identify the correct inverse of \( A \) that satisfies \( A \cdot A^{-1} = I \) and explain your reasoning.\n\nA)

