Let \(\vec{r}\) be a vector with a magnitude of 21 and direction ratios (DRs) 2, -3, and 6. If the direction cosines are all positive and the components are arranged accordingly, which of the following represents the correct vector \(\vec{r}\) in terms of \(\mathbf{i}, \mathbf{j}, \mathbf{k}\)?

